# Convex Real-time Patterns

## Core Concept

Convex `useQuery` is reactive by default. When the underlying data changes, the query re-runs and the component re-renders with fresh data. There is:

- No `useEffect` for subscriptions
- No manual channel setup or cleanup
- No event listeners (`INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`)
- No channel naming
- No `removeChannel` cleanup
- No missed events (guaranteed consistency)

## Before vs After

### OLD (Supabase) - Do NOT use this pattern
```typescript
// REMOVED: useEffect + postgres_changes subscription
useEffect(() => {
  const supabase = createClient();
  const channel = supabase
    .channel(`game_session_${gameId}`)
    .on("postgres_changes", { event: "*", table: "game_sessions", filter: `game_id=eq.${gameId}` },
      (payload) => setState(payload.new)
    )
    .subscribe();
  return () => supabase.removeChannel(channel);
}, [gameId]);
```

### NEW (Convex) - Use this pattern
```typescript
import { useQuery } from "convex/react";
import { api } from "@/convex/_generated/api";

// Single line. Auto-subscribes. Auto-updates. Auto-cleans up.
const gameSession = useQuery(api.gameSessions.getByGame, { gameId });
```

## Subscription Replacements

Every old Supabase realtime hook is replaced by a `useQuery` call:

| Old Hook (DELETED) | New Pattern |
|---|---|
| `useGameSessionListener` | `useQuery(api.gameSessions.getByGame, { gameId })` |
| `useGamePlayerListener` | `useQuery(api.gamePlayers.listByGame, { gameId })` |
| `useGameHostSubscription` | `useQuery(api.games.getById, { gameId })` then read `hostId` |
| `useNightPhaseSessionListener` | `useQuery(api.nightPhaseSessions.getCurrent, { gameId })` |
| `usePlayerRolesListener` | `useQuery(api.gamePlayerRoles.getFiltered, { gameId })` |
| `useMyJoinRequestStatus` | `useQuery(api.joinRequests.getMyStatus, { gameId })` |
| `usePendingJoinRequests` | `useQuery(api.joinRequests.listPending, { gameId })` |
| `useLobbySubscription` | `useQuery(api.games.listAll)` |

## Conditional Queries

Use `"skip"` to conditionally disable a query (replaces `enabled` flag):

```typescript
// Only subscribe when gameId is available
const session = useQuery(
  api.gameSessions.getByGame,
  gameId ? { gameId } : "skip"
);
```

## Loading States

`useQuery` returns `undefined` while loading:

```typescript
const gameSession = useQuery(api.gameSessions.getByGame, { gameId });

if (gameSession === undefined) {
  return <LoadingSpinner />;
}

// gameSession is now the actual data (or null if not found)
```

## Combining Multiple Queries

Call multiple `useQuery` hooks in the same component. Each subscribes independently:

```typescript
function GameRoom({ gameId }) {
  const game = useQuery(api.games.getById, { gameId });
  const session = useQuery(api.gameSessions.getByGame, { gameId });
  const players = useQuery(api.gamePlayers.listByGame, { gameId });
  const nightSession = useQuery(
    api.nightPhaseSessions.getCurrent,
    session?.gamePhase === "night_phase" ? { gameId } : "skip"
  );

  // All four queries auto-update independently when their data changes
}
```

## Writing Data (Mutations)

Mutations trigger reactive query updates automatically:

```typescript
const castVote = useMutation(api.votes.cast);

// When this mutation completes, any useQuery watching the votes table
// will automatically re-run and update the UI
await castVote({ votingSessionId, voterSeat: 3, seatNumber: 5 });
```

## No Separate Fetch + Subscribe

The old pattern of "fetch initial data then subscribe" is eliminated:

```typescript
// OLD (Supabase) - fetch + subscribe
useEffect(() => {
  fetchInitialData().then(setState);
  const channel = supabase.channel(...).subscribe();
  return () => supabase.removeChannel(channel);
}, []);

// NEW (Convex) - single useQuery does both
const data = useQuery(api.myTable.get, { id });
```

## Performance Notes

- Convex queries only re-run when the specific data they read changes
- No need to filter at the database level (Convex handles this efficiently)
- No need to debounce (Convex batches updates)
- No need to limit subscriptions (Convex manages connections)
- Convex automatically handles reconnection and catch-up after network issues
